   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to increasing\nfinancing for project costs of the Battery Park city authority",
    "basePrintNo": "S6411",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6411-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1977-a, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6411\n\nSPONSOR: KAVANAGH\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the public authorities law, in\nrelation to increasing financing for project costs of the Battery Park\ncity authority\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to amend the public authorities law to\nauthorize an increase in the allowed amount of outstanding debt for the\nfinancing of critical infrastructure and resiliency related projects in\nBattery Park.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends paragraph (a) of subsection 1 of section 1977-a of the\npublic authorities law to increase Battery Park City Authority's bonding\ncapacity from a maximum amount of three hundred million dollars to a\nmaximum amount of six hundred, fifty million dollars.\n\nSection 2. Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe current law caps the amount of debt that Battery Park City Authority\n(BPCA) may incur for purposes of financing project costs at three\nhundred million dollars. BPCA's capital plan outlines critical infras-\ntructure and resiliency related projects that must be completed post-Su-\nperstorm Sandy, but exceed the authority's available bonding capacity.\nThis bill proposes to allow for design and construction of these neces-\nsary projects by increasing BPCA's bonding authority to a maximum of six\nhundred, fifty million dollars. Revenues currently collected by BPCA are\nsufficient to support an increase in its annual debt service payments\ncaused by an increase in bond capacity.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNo State budget implications.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
