    "lawCode": "Amd §1977-a, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6411A\n\nSPONSOR: KAVANAGH\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the public authorities law, in\nrelation to the Battery Park city authority\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to amend the public authorities law to\nauthorize a non-renewable amount of debt for the financing of critical\ninfrastructure and resiliency related projects in Battery Park.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends paragraph (a) of subsection 1 of section 1977-a of\nthe public authorities law to provision Battery Park City Authority with\na non-revolving bonding capacity not to exceed five hundred million\ndollars.\n\nSection two sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nPURPOSE AND JUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrent law caps the amount of debt that Battery Park City Authority\n(BPCA) may incur for purposes of financing project costs at three\nhundred fifty million dollars. BPCA's capital plan outlines critical\ninfrastructure and resiliency related projects that must be completed\npost-Superstorm Sandy. However, these costs are expected to exceed the\nauthority's available renewable bonding capacity. This bill proposes to\nallow for design and construction of these necessary projects by provi-\nsioning the BPCA with a separate non-revolving bonding capacity not to\nexceed five hundred million dollars.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
